# the review at step 2 (JEVCODE_MOCK_REVIEW_AT=2) is approved with y (§6); the card is a rounded `╭─ review · step 2` card in
# the boxed tier (TUI-DESIGN-2 §4.7, §8.2 review-y (ext.)); Enter on the armed card is inert (§9 "review invariants": only
# `y` approves) — the smoke counts exactly one `confirm … approved` in transcript.log and no `› y` composer echo
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect Say hi
sleep 0.3
send make the tests pass
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect ╭─ (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*review · step 2
expect \[y\] approve
sleep 0.4
send \r
sleep 0.25
send y
expect confirm \S+ approved
expect end (complete|max_steps|generator_done)
expect Follow-up, question
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
